=== ARCHITECTURAL CORRECTIONS TO v4 ===

1. INPUT CONTRACT: ALA does NOT push full review data. The webhook payload to EIP is only: ala_record_id, prior_run_id, prior_table ("ALA"), lang ("en"/"es"), client_id. EIP re-fetches the full ALA record itself via a NocoDB GET (Step 3) — Platform, Date, Star Rating, Raw Text, Pain Point Domain, Preliminary Emotion Tag, Keywords, Reviewer Handle.

2. DUAL-LANGUAGE DICTIONARIES (undocumented in v4 entirely): EIP branches by resolved `lang` and selects one of two table pairs:
   - es → Emotion Dictionary table `mhot4w62tupht71` (161 rows, confirmed populated/clean), Pain Point Master table `mwmiyyoucuhsms8` (253 rows, confirmed populated/clean)
   - en (default) → Emotion Dictionary `mrrscb955j1d2i7`, Pain Point Master `meavqh37mdqgl4d` (336 rows per v4 — NOT re-verified this cycle, see Gaps below)

3. FULL NODE FLOW (29 nodes), in order:
   Webhook → Step 1 Payload Validation (requires positive-int ala_record_id) → Step 2 Idempotency Check/IF/Skip Duplicate/False Branch Gate (checks EIP table by ALA Record ID; duplicate branch dead-ends, no further routing) → Step 3 Fetch ALA Record → Step 3b ALA Validation (requires Raw Tex, Platform, Date, Pain Point Domain, Preliminary Emotion Tag; strips [N★] markers) → Step 4 Patch ALA Processing (sets EIP Status: Processing) → Step 5 Dictionary Load Check (resolves lang, picks table IDs) → Step 5 INIT 1-4 (fetch + serialize Emotion Dictionary and Pain Point Master, language-branched field names, builds signal_weight_map) → Step 6 Build GPT Prompt (ALA's own domain/emotion passed as context-only hints, not authoritative) → Step 7 Build GPT Request Body (model gpt-5.2, temperature 0.2, max_completion_tokens 600, response_format json_object) → Step 8 GPT Classification Call (NO retry-on-fail configured) → Step 9 Output Parsing (validates emotion fields/enums, clamps polarity/certainty to [0,1], caps certainty at 0.40 if tag looks numeric/bracketed, looks up signal_weight) → Step 10 Signal Type → STEP 11 Semantic Collapse Detection → Step 12 Ambiguity Flag (threshold 0.65) → STEP 13 Run ID + Timestamp (format EIP-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-mmm) → Step 14 Build NocoDB Body → STEP 15 NocoDB POST (writes EIP record) → Step 16 Capture EIP Record ID (throws if no Id returned) → Step 17/17a Patch ALA Complete (sets EIP Status: Complete) → Step 18/18a ESS Trigger (fires webhook to ESS, NO onError fallback configured).

4. SIGNAL TYPE (Step 10) — v4's documented T-NEGATIVE/T-AMBIGUOUS/T-POSITIVE taxonomy does NOT match the live code. Actual logic produces one of six values based on dominant_pole, masked_emotion_flag, certainty_score, and emotion_category:
   - Positive Signal (pole = Positive)
   - Masked Negative Signal (pole = Negative, masked = true)
   - Ambiguous Negative Signal (pole = Negative, certainty < 0.65)
   - Dignity-Risk Signal (pole = Negative, emotion_category text-matches "Relational"/"Identity"/"Dignity"/"Trust")
   - Negative Signal (pole = Negative, none of the above)
   - Mixed Signal (pole = Mixed)
   Document this as the actual current logic, explicitly superseding v4's taxonomy.

5. NOCODB SCHEMA (table mhicpnrahaesxmy) — actual fields written by Step 14: EIP Run ID, ALA Record ID, EIP Timestamp, Enriched Emotion Tag, Enriched Pain Point, Domain, Intensity Level, Polarity Balance, Dominant Pole, Certainty Score, Ambiguity Flag, Collapse flag, Masked Emotion Flag, Cognitive Driver, Need State, Signal Type, Emotion Hypothesis, Pain Hypothesis, Keywords, Signal Weight, Client ID, ESS Status, Error Log. v4's documented "Enriched Emotion Breakdown", "Enriched Pain Point Breakdown" (JSON arrays), and standalone "Core Emotion" column do NOT appear in the actual write payload — remove or flag as unconfirmed.

